FamilyTree.person({"id":"desiderius_dk","name":"Desiderius De Keyser","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"De Keyser","family":"dekeyser","died":"","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"mtheresia_vandenbroeck","name":"Maria Theresia Van den Broeck"}],"source":"Édouard Dekeyser's 1946 Oostende remarriage act (akte nr. 81); FamilySearch","note":"Source detail: Oostende marriage act nr. 81, 9 May 1946 (FamilySearch, Belgium West Flanders Civil Registration 1582-1950 — image read directly), naming him as father of Eduardus De Keyser\n\nFATHER of Édouard Dekeyser — the long-sought wall, now broken. Named (with his wife) in Édouard's 1946 remarriage act as 'zoon van Desiderius en van Maria Theresia Van den Broeck, beiden overleden'. A Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) family (his son Mauritius Eduardus married in Hamme in 1912; his son Édouard was born in Hamme in 1876). Both parents were already deceased by 9 May 1946. Their known children (FamilySearch, Oost-Vlaanderen civil registration): Édouard (1876, our line), Mauritius Eduardus (1892, m. Marie Henriette Neus, Hamme 1912), Augustinus (†1883 as an infant), Frederiens Carolus, and Leontinus Josephus de Keyser. His own dates/parents are the new frontier — pursue in the Hamme (O.-Vl.) registers (AGATHA / FamilySearch)."});
