FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_f","name":"Petrus Franciscus Bundervoet","dates":"19 Mar 1879 Evergem – 21 Jul 1943 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"19 Mar 1879 Evergem","died":"21 Jul 1943 Oostende","occupation":"werkman / meestergast","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"bernardus","mother":"goethals","spouses":[{"id":"augusta","name":"Augusta Vanstechelman"}],"source":"Geneanet","note":"The FIRST of the Bundervoet line to leave Evergem for the coast: born in Evergem, he settled in Oostende, where all his children were born from 1905 onward. Married Augusta Vanstechelman (the Bundervoet–Vanstechelman junction). FRONTIER (MyHeritage, July 2026): two independent Bundervoet family trees on MyHeritage — one run by Lucien Bundervoet, one by Johny Henricus Bundervoet, both in Belgium — agree that he and Augusta had SIX children, not the one recorded here: Alphons Bernardus Cyprianus, Emilius Josephus, Achilles, Henricus Eduardus, Irena Augusta and Camillus Edmundus. The same trees give him at least four siblings, one named Maria Bundervoet. His own birth and death match ours exactly (19 Mar 1879 Evergem, 21 Jul 1943), which is what makes the match credible. NOT GRAFTED: member trees are not records and no dates for the children were readable, so the five siblings need their Oostende birth acts (1905 onward) before they go in."});
