FamilyTree.person({"id":"simon_vandewalle_1565","name":"Simon Vandewalle","dates":"~1565 Oostkamp – 28 Jul 1636 Oostkamp","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","born":"~1565 Oostkamp","died":"28 Jul 1636 Oostkamp","occupation":"koster / landman (church sexton / farmer)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"simon_vandewalle_1530","mother":"joanna_wittenheyns","spouses":[{"id":"christina_desangere","name":"Christina Desangere"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Sexton (koster) of Oostkamp church and a Bruges citizen; grave inscription survives in the church. In a 1635 deed he swore he was born in Oostkamp and was then 70 (=> b. ~1565). Extensive property records 1597-1621."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"simonne","name":"Simonne Vandewalle","dates":"b. 1913–1914 Oostende?","confidence":"fam","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","born":"1913–1914 Oostende?","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"gustaaf","name":"Gustaaf Dekeyser"}],"source":"Geneanet; The family itself","note":"Source detail: Family (confirmed maiden name). Oostende candidates: Simonne Florida Vandewalle 1913 & Simonne Augusta 1914 — West-Vlaanderen civil birth acts (Geneanet)\n\nRESEARCH NOTE. Vandewalle is one of the most common West-Flemish surnames, so isolating her needs a linking record. Two strong Oostende candidates of the right age: (a) Simonne Florida Vandewalle, b. 6 Jun 1913 Oostende — parents Petrus Franciscus Antonius Vandewalle (1884) & Magdalena Clementia Willaert (1888); grandparents Franciscus Eduardus Vandewalle × Mathildis Vandierendounck and Emilius Willaert (1856) × Maria Lauwereins (1856–1893); (b) Simonne Augusta Vandewalle, b. 1914 Oostende. Neither is yet tied to Gustaaf. Decisive record: the Gustaaf × Simonne marriage (Oostende ~1938–40, or England 1940–43) — it would name her parents — or Roland’s 1943 UK birth (mother’s maiden name)."});
