FamilyTree.person({"id":"thiery_f","name":"François Thumas","dates":"b. 1930–1939","confidence":"fam","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"1930–1939","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"jean_t","mother":"crabbe","spouses":[{"id":"juliette","name":"Juliette Vandenhoeck"}],"source":"The family itself","note":"Named by the family. His father is almost certainly Jean Thumas (1907–1995), who stayed in Kraainem — and Jean’s wife was Marie Louise Crabbé, so she is François’s mother. This father-link falls inside the 100-year privacy window and is the only remaining inference. Everything above it is documented: Jean → J.B. Georgius (1876) → Georges Carolus Josephus (1836) → the Grez-Doiceau Thumas trunk back to 1656."});
